<title>TANZANIA: Tanzania bans meat imports due to mad cow fears.</title>
<headline>Tanzania bans meat imports due to mad cow fears.</headline>
<dateline>DAR ES SALAAM 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tanzania has banned the importation of beef, pork and meat products from Britain, Ireland, France, Switzerland and Portugal because of mad cow disease.</p>
<p>The agriculture ministry ordered the ban on Sunday and told shops and supermarkets to remove from shelves and destroy stocks of frozen beef, pork and meat products imported from the five countries.</p>
<p>The ministry said skimmed milk from the five countries would still be allowed into Tanzania but beef, pork and meat products that were imported from all other countries should first be certified by health authorities in their country of origin.</p>
<p>They should certify that any frozen beef, corned beef and other products were only from cattle from the country of origin.</p>
<p>The European Union banned beef exports from Britain in March because of the risk from bovine spongiform encephalopathy or &quot;mad cow&quot; disease.</p>
<p>The Tanzanian agriculture ministry said it had decided to ban meat imports from all countries reported hit by the disease. It was not clear why there was a delay in announcing the ban.</p>
